==English==

===Etymology===
Late 14th century, from {{etyl|frm}} {{term|posterité|lang=frm}}, from {{etyl|la}} {{term|posteritas|lang=la}}, from {{term|posterus||following, coming after|lang=la}}, from {{term|post||after|lang=la}} ({{etyl|en|-}} {{term|post-|lang=en}}).<ref>{{R:Online Etymology Dictionary}}</ref>

Displaced Old English words such as {{term|æftercneoreso|lang=ang}}, {{term|frumcynn|lang=ang}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈpɒstɛɹɪti/}} {{X-SAMPA|/"pQstErIti:/}}
* {{audio|en-us-posterity.ogg|Audio (US)}}

* {{rhymes|ɪti}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# All the [[future]] [[generation]]s, especially the [[descendant]]s of a [[specific]] person.

